From e26e4082ac30f7f36d648a860f09b3705d8804b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-v5 <v5@localhost>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 17:53:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] v5: DCE-after-vectorize, reduction-loop register reuse,
 scalar-FP XMM codegen

Auto-vectorizer (fixes the v4 DCE gap):
- run DCE immediately after vectorization, before IVSR: the orphaned scalar
  load/mul/GEP chains were strength-reduced into dead loop-carried pointer
  increments (leaq 256(%rdi),%rdi) that the later DCE could not remove.

Reduction hot-loop codegen:
- VecLoad reuses register-allocated base/offset GPRs (no movq-to-rax/rcx).
- accumulator phi group {acc, init_zero, vec_sum} now coalesces to one home
  slot via CFG copy-coalescing (removes the per-iteration accumulator
  slot-to-slot copy): SUM 8->6, DOT 11->9 instructions/iteration.

Scalar FP XMM codegen (systemic; FP values were GPR round-tripped):
- F64 register pool keeps xmm2 unless the function contains an intrinsic that
  clobbers it (pblendvb/128-bit VNNI/F128), instead of unconditionally
  dropping it (that caused spills and a 3x nbody slowdown).
- FP binary ops now honor XMM-register homes for LHS and dest (was RHS-only).
- int->float casts emit cvtsi2sd/cvtsi2ss straight into the dest register.
- F64/F32 loads emit movsd/movss (%ptr), %xmmN straight into the dest register.

Measured: spectral_norm 9.3x -> 3.5x vs gcc; reduction loops down to 6/9
instructions; nbody/mandelbrot correct (bit-exact vs gcc).
Validation: regression 127/127, correctness 50/50, intrinsics 3/3, reduction
difftests 0..300 x {AVX2,SSE2} bit-exact, zlib-ng adler32 correct.
