the result straight into that register (LHS -> dest reg, RHS folded/register,
op into dest reg), instead of the xmm0-scratch + store-to-home + reload-from-
home sequence. Halves the per-link register moves in scalar FP chains.

Measured (min-of-4, pinned, vs gcc):
- spectral_norm  9.3x -> 2.9x  (was 1.75s, now 0.62s)
- struct_copy    20.9x -> 6.7x (0.60s -> 0.20s)
- nbody          11.9x -> 4.8x (3.7s -> 1.5s, broken measurement fixed)
- mandelbrot     2.9x (unchanged; compare/branch bound)

Correctness: nbody/spectral_norm/mandelbrot bit-exact vs gcc; regression
127/127, correctness 50/50, intrinsics 3/3.
